<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71269" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leader of the bride,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				610
			</span></i> ; esp. <i>one who leads her from her home to the
				bridegroom's house,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				20.16
			</span></i> ; esp. in case of a second marriage, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				652.45
			</span></i> : metaph., of the Argo, as bearing Medea, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. τρόπιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					1025
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>friend,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				21.22
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Jd.</u>
				14.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who negotiates a marriage for another,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.329f
			</span></i>. Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νυμφευτής.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
